      "message": "I\u0027m sorry, but I\u0027m not seeing the difference.\n\nMy perspective is:\n\"I need to run on Linux\" is not that different from \"I need to be in S0\". The only difference is that there\u0027s a utility to make that happen. if the code that changes the power state ends up with a bug, we shouldn\u0027t fail _EVERY_ test that used the utility just for \"needing to be in S0\"",
